- Existing Java command fixtures use placeholder `oracle` extFields and do not constitute typed-header oracle fixtures. P4-V01 remains open; continue by adding a real source-backed Java header fixture generator and Rust/Java cross-decode assertions.
- First functional commit: `0195fd8 feat(protocol): add typed core remoting headers`.
- Work continues; Phase 4 not complete.

## First-wave implementation status
- Commits: `0195fd8` core typed headers; `f251dd4` optional presence semantics; `a39d5a2` routing/consumer lock models.
- Added Java 5.5.1 typed header fixture generation for route, send V1/V2, pull request/response, query offset request/response, update offset, send response, and consumer-list request. Metadata marks Java 5.5.1; raw frames stored in `fixtures/remoting/`.
